{"name":"Blue Overdose","hex":"#0020ef","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"overdose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An excessive and dangerous dose of a drug."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dose to excess; to give an overdose, or too many doses, to someone.","To dose excessively, to take an overdose."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overdose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drug overdose","blocks":[{"text":"A drug overdose is the ingestion or application of a drug or other substance in quantities much greater than are recommended. Typically the term is applied for cases when a risk to health is a potential result. An overdose may result in a toxic state or death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/DrugOverdose.jpg/330px-DrugOverdose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drug_overdose","wikidata":"Q3505252"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/CharcoalPO.jpg/500px-CharcoalPO.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/CharcoalPO.jpg/1280px-CharcoalPO.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/CharcoalPO.jpg/500px-CharcoalPO.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Activated charcoal is a commonly used agent for decontamination of the gastrointestinal tract in overdoses.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharcoalPO.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Overdose_or_drug-related_death_rate_per_1_million_population_%28unadjusted%29%2C_2022%2C_by_country_or_region.png/500px-Overdose_or_drug-related_death_rate_per_1_million_population_%28unadjusted%29%2C_2022%2C_by_country_or_region.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Overdose_or_drug-related_death_rate_per_1_million_population_%28unadjusted%29%2C_2022%2C_by_country_or_region.png/1280px-Overdose_or_drug-related_death_rate_per_1_million_population_%28unadjusted%29%2C_2022%2C_by_country_or_region.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Overdose_or_drug-related_death_rate_per_1_million_population_%28unadjusted%29%2C_2022%2C_by_country_or_region.png/500px-Overdose_or_drug-rel